{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Jethro, Moses' father-in-law, took a burnt-offering and sacrifices for Elohim.</b> All of this was before they came to Mount Sinai. It is also possible to explain that Scripture arranged the entire account of Jethro in sequence, but this was after he stayed with them many days, and he converted through circumcision and immersion and the bringing of blood, according to the ordinance." "<b>And Aaron came, and all the elders of Israel, to eat bread</b> with him on the day of his wedding-feast, for he is a bridegroom of blood."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "הַרְצָאַת דָּמִים literally 'bringing/approach of blood,' a technical term for the blood-rites of conversion; rendered literally.", 1 "כִּי חֲתַן דָּמִים הוּא echoes Exodus 4:25-26; the phrase left as Ramban cites it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:10:29.976755884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}